PROJECT_MEMORY/v1
status: PARKED
execution_authorized: false
portfolio: Mindrock Operating System
project_name: Agentic GAAP & State Positions

# Founding thesis

In an agentic corporation, inference resources can be managed with accounting-style disciplines analogous to budgeting, accrual, variance, reserves, functional currency, utilization and management reporting — while explicitly avoiding the claim that this system itself constitutes statutory GAAP compliance.

Different model/provider token pools are distinct resource currencies. Local Ollama/Gemma, Gemini Free Tier, OpenAI/Codex and future providers may have different scarcity, quality, latency, expiration, privacy and replacement-cost characteristics.

# Inference Treasury / accounting layer

Define provider/model resource ledgers with at least:
- opening capacity/budget;
- committed capacity;
- actual consumed capacity;
- reserved capacity;
- expiring unused capacity;
- backlog demand;
- variance vs plan;
- realized evidence/value output;
- provider/model quality and reliability history.

Candidate internal functional unit: a provider-neutral shadow value / replacement-cost unit rather than pretending raw tokens are fungible.

Key invariant:
`resource accounting != money accounting`, but accounting discipline can be reused.

# Show-Me-The-Money operational control

Every material inference spend should be attributable:
`org -> portfolio -> project -> task -> claim -> inference -> evidence/value transition`.

SMTM is two-sided:
- Project requesting capacity: `show me the expected value transition`;
- SmartRouter/Treasury with expiring surplus: `show me the backlog`.

Under-utilization is a management signal when useful positive-value backlog should exist.

# Four-quadrant resource SLA

1. Important + Critical = immediate execution / protected capacity.
2. Important + Non-critical = strategic reserve backlog; preferred consumer of spare/expiring capacity.
3. Non-important + Critical = assist opportunistically without displacing protected important work.
4. Non-important + Non-critical = self-development, learning, internal experiments, optional residual capacity.

Hypothesis: Q2 is the principal organizational inefficiency in conventional operations because strategically important but non-urgent work repeatedly loses to urgency. SmartRouter should explicitly protect a capacity corridor for Q2 rather than allocate only by urgency.

Golden-ratio / ~60% operating corridor is a hypothesis to test, not a fixed policy: normal planned load below saturation preserves burst optionality; unused reserve gradually becomes available to Q2/backfill as expiry approaches.

# Management dashboard / SLA backpropagation

Internal dashboard target update cadence: near-real-time / minute-scale where telemetry permits.
Public LP/investor projection may be delayed/redacted (e.g. ~1 hour) to protect operational/security-sensitive details.

Traffic-light semantics must be mechanically grounded:
- GREEN: within accepted budget/SLA/project-gate tolerances; backlog depth healthy;
- YELLOW: measurable variance, lag or forecast miss requiring local correction;
- RED: blocked/stalled, repeated no-progress loop, violated hard SLA, or problem requires escalation to a higher authority/abstraction level.

Candidate metrics:
- budget vs actual inference by resource currency and normalized shadow value;
- backlog coverage horizon by Project/Portfolio;
- SLA uptime/reliability;
- acceptance-gate movement;
- PR/evidence lag;
- blocked duration / restart-without-state-change count;
- useful evidence per inference spend;
- Q2 strategic backlog aging;
- provider quota utilization and expiry forecast.

RED alerts may escalate to CEO/Managing Partner/Compliance according to explicit severity and human-presence policy. External LP dashboard must distinguish honest problem disclosure from operational control rights and must redact secrets/private project data.

# State Positions: agentic headcount inversion

Conventional corporations minimize headcount partly because each position has continuous salary/benefit cost and often adds sequential gatekeeping latency.

Agentic hypothesis: a dormant narrow specialist can have near-zero marginal idle inference cost. Therefore a very large agentic org chart may improve coverage and reduce decision latency if activation is event-driven and authority remains explicit.

Define `STATE_POSITION/v1` as an addressable dormant organizational role, not a continuously-running LLM process.

Minimal position record:
- stable role/position id;
- org/portfolio/department/manager path;
- verb/domain specialization;
- semantic fingerprints / trigger predicates;
- authority/capabilities;
- budget class;
- SLA/escalation path;
- privacy/compliance constraints;
- role memory/provenance refs;
- current lifecycle state;
- wake cost and preferred inference substrate.

Dormant representation should be compact (manifest + semantic index/DHT entry). Full model context is materialized only on wake.

# Example specialist

`Ministry of External Relations -> Strategic Partners -> Google/Gemini -> Access & Resource Manager`.

This role may remain dormant for months/years, yet wake when a new issue exhibits a familiar invariant: credential enrollment, free-quota availability, provider account ambiguity, secret-exposure loop, or provider policy mismatch.

# Semantic self-nomination

Events/problems are fingerprinted by behavior/verb/invariant, not only topic keywords.

Target path:
`Problem/Event -> Semantic Fingerprint -> Specialist Registry/DHT -> candidate State Positions -> CAN/MAY/WILL/GUARD -> wake -> Claim/Evidence`.

A specialist may self-nominate when a new problem collides with a known invariant from a different domain (e.g. Meta credential loop resembles prior Google credential loop).

# Detective / Compliance integration

Detective watches for repeated no-progress/restart loops, stale states and forgotten evidence.
When a loop exceeds threshold without material state change, Detective/Compliance should search the State Position registry for specialists whose prior solved invariants match the current problem.

# Butterfly / research hypothesis

BUTTERFLY/v1
symptom: conventional intuition says thousands of narrowly-scoped corporate positions are bureaucratic bloat.
integration_context: agent positions consume little/no inference while dormant but can provide immediate specialized response when semantically triggered.
cocoon: `headcount` is the wrong denominator for agentic organizations; the relevant costs are active inference, coordination, wake precision, authority checks and decision latency.
candidate_transformation: replace headcount minimization with `coverage density / active decision cost / value per inference / latency / false-wake rate` optimization.
cheapest_falsification: replay a historical issue corpus through (A) one generalist + skills.md and (B) a registry of dormant specialist State Positions, holding model quality roughly constant. Measure routing accuracy, relevant-specialist recall, false wakes, cost, time-to-useful-evidence, authority errors and outcome quality.
status: research candidate

# Key risks / falsifiers

- coordination overhead grows faster than specialist benefit;
- semantic routing wakes too many wrong agents;
- stale specialist knowledge causes harmful confident actions;
- responsibility becomes diffuse;
- narrow roles create policy conflicts or deadlocks;
- authority graph becomes harder to audit than a simpler skill system;
- token/context materialization dominates the claimed idle-cost advantage.

Negative result is valuable: if large State Position graphs underperform a small number of generalists with skills, report `SCIENTIFIC_NEGATIVE`, not execution failure.

# Candidate research successor

`AGENTIC-HEADCOUNT-0001`: build a controlled simulation using historical Mindrock/ChitAkasha issue patterns. Compare generalist-skill architecture vs 10/100/1000 dormant State Positions on semantic routing, wake rate, decision latency, cost, evidence quality and authority safety. Include at least one cross-domain transfer case analogous to Google -> Meta credential-loop recognition.

# Governance principle

A State Position is an organizational address and policy-bearing latent capability, not proof that an agent is continuously alive or thinking. Position existence must not imply execution authority outside its CAN/MAY/WILL/GUARD contract.

