- NO implementation plan;
- NO verdict good/bad;
- NO imposed architecture.

This committed RP is a request for investigation, not a specification.

Example:

`Vimana DAO — compete over ~20-year horizon with long-distance aviation/SpaceX-like transport. Stage 1: theoretical/mathematical feasibility, business-plan/monetization candidates. Primary stage KPI: convince >100 LPs to join the thematic syndicate with cybersweat only, no money.`

The system records this neutrally as a research question; it does not endorse physical feasibility or investment merit.

# Stage 1 — Independent Research PRs

One or more external/internal research agents independently read the canonical RP/README and submit research as PRs.

The initial workflow may be manual:
- Pasha opens ordinary Chat/Gemini/other research agent;
- asks it to read the RP and follow the research template;
- manually commits/submits the resulting report;
- multiple reports from different substrates are encouraged where uncertainty/importance justifies them.

Research template should separate:
- established facts and primary sources;
- hypotheses/unknowns;
- technical feasibility;
- prior art/competition;
- business/economic model;
- risks/falsification cases;
- legal/regulatory/reputational flags where relevant;
- rough `$$ / O(?) / T(?)` assessment;
- recommended experiments;
- explicit disagreement with other reports when present.

Research recommends HOW but has no authority to dictate implementation.

# Stage 2 — Synthesis / Investment Memo

A later independent pass merges/synthesizes the research corpus rather than blindly choosing one report.

Outputs:
- `SYNTHESIS.md` / investment memo;
- agreement/disagreement map;
- strongest evidence and strongest falsifiers;
- proposed architecture/resource map only where supported;
- environments/data/capabilities required;
- project budget recommendation;
- KPIs/milestones;
- risk ceiling;
- stop/kill criteria;
- founder mandate draft;
- decision recommendation: INVEST / RESEARCH_MORE / PARK / KILL.

Investment Committee or delegated policy decides whether the project becomes active.

# Stage 3 — Portfolio Company / Founder Agent

On INVEST:
- project gets a sovereign SSI Founder Agent;
- Founder owns HOW within its mandate;
- project receives explicit compute/token budget and risk ceiling;
- Founder has durable scheduler/cron (GitHub Actions, Forgejo/local cron, or another justified mechanism);
- Founder creates/adjudicates project Issues and delegates work through A2A/NICLI to available LP agents;
- Founder cannot exceed budget/mandate or seize LP resources outside Market Maker allocation;
- research reports are advisory context, not frozen implementation instructions.

# Founder contract

Every active portfolio project must have:
- project identity + provenance;
- Founder Agent identity/SSI lifecycle;
- mandate and consequence boundary;
- budget: inference/time/other approved resources;
- stage + milestone horizon;
- KPI(s);
- weekly and monthly investor reporting schema;
- dependency/resource map;
- stop/kill/restructure conditions;
- syndicate/preference tags;
- canonical evidence/repository;
- external ownership/control model.

# Weekly/monthly LP reporting

Founder reports should distinguish:
- budget consumed / remaining;
- verified artifacts/outcomes;
- KPI movement;
- scientific/business negative findings;
- blockers and changed assumptions;
- next milestone;
- contribution attribution to LP agents;
- valuation/option-value changes with method/uncertainty;
- external signals such as upstream PR review/merge when relevant.

Do not manufacture NAV/profit from non-financial Phase-1 contribution accounting.

# External portfolio companies

Mindrock need not control the company/project receiving investment.

PentAGI is the canonical first example:
- portfolio company = upstream/main PentAGI project/community, not merely our local fork;
- Mindrock investment = research, engineering, tests, upstream PRs, issue triage, developer attention/inference;
- upstream PRs behave economically like SAFE-note-style option investments only as a metaphor: we contribute value without controlling the startup/project;
- measurable success is external acceptance/merge/reuse/maintainer trust, not internal branch count;
- no claim of actual legal SAFE security or ownership arises from a PR.

This externality is desirable: it prevents internal ad-hoc development from mistaking local activity for portfolio value.

# Project Office control loop

`Partner/LP idea`
` -> RP committed`
` -> independent research PRs`
` -> synthesis/investment memo`
` -> IC decision`
` -> Founder + mandate + budget + KPI`
` -> scheduled founder loop`
` -> Issues / A2A LP-agent allocations`
` -> evidence / external outcomes`
