# Purpose

Define Prometheus as the local sovereign execution/feedback plane that does not depend on OpenAI scheduler availability and keeps private intellectual property, operational memory, and emergency feedback under local control.

This is durable project memory, not an executable task. Never CLAIM it directly.

# Role

Prometheus is not another cloud scheduler persona. It is the local nervous system beneath the Mindrock organization:

- runs from local infrastructure with its own independent cron/event scheduler;
- can observe local agent execution and structured blocker telemetry;
- persists private project/IP state locally;
- maintains a direct emergency feedback path to Pasha;
- can continue collecting evidence and preserving continuity when cloud scheduler/quota is unavailable;
- must not silently inherit cloud authority merely because it is local.

# Storage hypothesis

Candidate architecture:

`local agents / executors`
`        ↓`
`Prometheus event + evidence bus`
`        ↓`
`local append-only content-addressed store`
`        ↓`
`Arweave-compatible/L2-style persistence or another measured local permanent-log design`

"Arweave L2" is currently a design hypothesis/name, not a claim that a production Arweave layer-2 implementation already exists locally. The actual storage substrate must be selected by evidence.

Requirements when activated:
- append-only/provenance-friendly semantics;
- content addressing and integrity proofs;
- encrypted/private-by-default payloads;
- local indexing/search;
- deterministic export/publication boundary;
- no accidental public replication of private IP;
- survivable restart/recovery;
- clear separation between evidence durability and semantic settlement authority.

# Scheduler independence

Prometheus should have a local event model such as cron/launchd plus durable queue rather than depending on ChatGPT scheduler.

Candidate trigger classes:
- periodic health/reconciliation;
- execution finished without settlement;
- repeated blocker signature;
- local service failure;
- quota/external-provider unavailability;
- expiring local lease/certificate;
- explicit emergency condition.

Do not turn every event into a Pasha notification. Escalate only when the configured consequence/urgency threshold is met.

# Direct emergency channel

The design should distinguish:

- normal durable Git/local event — no interruption;
- urgent operational notification — bounded push/channel;
- sovereign AUTH_REQUEST — requires Pasha action;
- emergency stop/containment — fail closed and preserve evidence.

The exact notification transport is a separate implementation decision; no credential or public endpoint is authorized by this memory node.

# Relationship to other projects

- #101 defines Prometheus blocker intelligence / feedback semantics.
- #100 SSI should eventually authenticate Prometheus and issue narrow local capabilities.
- #102 defines the organizational authority structure in which Prometheus is infrastructure, not Managing Director.
- #79 recovery work supplies regression cases for durable evidence before settlement.
- existing local Git/Forgejo/CAS work may provide reusable storage/provenance pieces and should be inspected before inventing a new stack.

# Candidate first bounded successor

`PROMETHEUS-LOCAL-0001 — local event/evidence journal with restart-safe synthetic triggers`

Observable result:
- local-only append-only event journal;
- deterministic hash/provenance chain;
- one cron/launchd synthetic periodic trigger;
- one synthetic execution-failure trigger;
- restart recovery;
- explicit demonstration that no private payload leaves the host and that journal events cannot mark a task completed.

No production emergency notifications or public Arweave publication in the first experiment.

# Long-term success

Prometheus gives the entire organization an independent local memory, pulse, diagnostic reflex, and emergency path while cloud agents remain replaceable and quota-constrained.

